@* Redirects to another route on first render.

   Used where a URL used to be a page of its own and is now somewhere else: the app root ("/")
   and the old diagnostics path ("/diag"). A redirect rather than a second @page on the target,
   so the old address stops being a place that can drift away from the page it stands for.

   replace: true, because the old address is not a history entry the user should be able to
   step back to — Back should land where they were before, not on the address that redirects
   to where they were before. *@

@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@code {
    /// <summary>Where to send the visitor.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string To { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(To))
            Navigation.NavigateTo(To, replace: true);
    }
}
